{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 15, :comments ["<b>And he saw the rest.</b> When he saw that his land and his resting place were pleasant, he bent his shoulder to bear every burden, as the donkey bears, and became as a servant who pays tribute. This is the meaning concerning Issachar, that they were not warriors, nor did they wish to go out to war and abandon their place. So too Moses said, \"And Issachar in your tents\" (Deuteronomy 33:18), and they would pay tribute to the king of Israel so that he would not go out, or to the nations so that they would not come to fight against them."], :book :genesis, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 49, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"] ["Piotrkow, 1907-1911" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH990020973480205171/NLI"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:48:28.533418546Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}